# Session 1 — Setup

Welcome! This week we set up your workshop. No real coding yet — just getting all the tools working.

## What's new this week

- Your project folder exists.
- You have Python, VS Code, Git, and your AI coding assistant installed.
- You have a free Gemini API key saved in `.env`.
- You can run a Streamlit app (even a tiny one!) on your own computer.

## What you'll learn

- What tools real AI developers use
- How to install Python, VS Code, and Git
- How to get a free API key from Google AI Studio
- What an API key is and why you keep it secret

## How to run it

**Step 1.** Install Python 3.10 or newer from [python.org](https://www.python.org/downloads/).
*(On macOS, you can also use `brew install python`. On Windows, check "Add Python to PATH" when installing.)*

**Step 2.** Install [VS Code](https://code.visualstudio.com/).

**Step 3.** Install [Git](https://git-scm.com/downloads).

**Step 4.** Get a free Gemini API key:
1. Go to [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com/).
2. Sign in with a Google account.
3. Click **Get API key** → **Create API key**.
4. Copy the key.

**Step 5.** In this folder, create a file called `.env` (same shape as `.env.example`) and paste:

```
GOOGLE_API_KEY=paste_your_key_here
```

**Step 6.** Open Terminal (macOS) or PowerShell (Windows), `cd` into this folder, and run:

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate       # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
streamlit run app.py
```

A browser tab should open at `http://localhost:8501`. You should see **"My Study Buddy"** as a page title.

🎉 Congrats — your toolchain works!

## What to try

1. **Change the title.** Open `app.py` in VS Code. Change `"My Study Buddy"` to something like `"Bea's Study Buddy"`. Save. Refresh the browser. Did it change? That's your first code edit!
2. **Add an emoji.** Try `st.title("My Study Buddy 📚")`.
3. **Write your concept sheet.** On paper or in a doc, answer three questions:
   - **Who** is my study buddy for? (yourself? your younger sibling? a friend?)
   - **What AI topic** do you want it to help with most? (prompting? neural networks? AI ethics?)
   - **One thing** it has to do really well? (explain concepts? quiz me? summarize my notes?)

We'll use your answers next week when we bring the AI to life.

## Common problems

**"`python` command not found"** — On some systems, it's `python3` instead of `python`. Try `python3 -m venv .venv`.

**"streamlit: command not found"** — You probably didn't activate the virtual environment. Run `source .venv/bin/activate` (or the Windows version) and you should see `(.venv)` at the start of your terminal line.

**"port 8501 is already in use"** — Another Streamlit app is running. Close it, or run `streamlit run app.py --server.port 8502`.
